{% load static %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <meta name="description" content="sbomify platform notification">
        <meta name="keywords"
              content="sbomify, sbom, software bill of materials, security">
        <title>
            {% block title %}sbomify{% endblock %}
        </title>
        <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
        <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
        {% comment %}
        Figtree is the app's typeface. Apple Mail and iOS load it; Gmail and
        Outlook ignore web fonts and fall through to the system stack.
        {% endcomment %}
        <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Figtree:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
              rel="stylesheet">
        {% comment %}
        Mail clients cannot read CSS custom properties, so the design tokens are
        written out as hex. Every value is the light theme's token from
        sbomify/assets/css/tailwind.src.css, named alongside it, and
        test_email_palette.py fails on one that is not. Change a token there,
        change it here.
        {% endcomment %}
        <style>
            body {
                font-family: 'Figtree', system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
                line-height: 1.6;
                color: #51546b; /* --color-text-secondary */
                margin: 0;
                padding: 0;
                background-color: #eef0f4; /* --color-surface-hover */
                -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
            }

            .email-wrapper {
                background-color: #eef0f4; /* --color-surface-hover */
            }

            .email-container {
                background-color: #ffffff; /* --color-surface */
                border: 1px solid #e9eaec; /* --color-border */
                border-radius: 12px; /* --radius-xl */
                overflow: hidden;
            }

            .email-body {
                padding: 40px;
            }

            .logo-cell {
                background-color: #25293f; /* --color-navy */
                padding: 24px;
                text-align: center;
            }

            .tagline-cell {
                background-color: #25293f; /* --color-navy */
                padding: 0 24px 20px 24px;
                text-align: center;
                color: #d3d4d9; /* --color-primary-lighter */
                font-size: 14px;
            }

            h1 {
                color: #25293f; /* --color-text */
                font-size: 24px;
                line-height: 1.3;
                margin-top: 0;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            h2 {
                color: #25293f; /* --color-text */
                font-size: 20px;
                margin-top: 32px;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            h3 {
                color: #25293f; /* --color-text */
                font-size: 18px;
                margin-bottom: 12px;
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            p {
                margin-top: 16px;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
                color: #51546b; /* --color-text-secondary */
            }

            strong {
                color: #25293f; /* --color-text */
            }

            ul {
                margin-top: 16px;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
                padding-left: 24px;
                color: #51546b; /* --color-text-secondary */
            }

            li {
                margin-top: 8px;
                margin-bottom: 8px;
            }

            /* The app's primary button on the light theme: a navy fill under
               white text. Clients that drop the gradient keep the solid fill. */
            a.button {
                display: inline-block;
                padding: 12px 24px;
                background-color: #25293f; /* --color-primary-fill */
                background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, #25293f 0%, #1a1d2e 100%); /* --color-primary-fill, -end */
                border: 0.5px solid #25293f; /* --color-primary */
                border-radius: 8px; /* --radius-lg */
                color: #ffffff;
                text-decoration: none;
                margin-top: 16px;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
                font-weight: 500;
                font-size: 15px;
                text-align: center;
            }

            .text-secondary {
                color: #6e7180; /* --color-text-muted */
                font-size: 14px;
            }

            .highlight-box {
                background-color: #eaeefd; /* --color-info-light */
                border-left: 3px solid #3e5ddd; /* --color-info */
                border-radius: 8px; /* --radius-lg */
                padding: 16px;
                margin-top: 24px;
                margin-bottom: 24px;
            }

            .feature-list {
                list-style: none;
                padding-left: 0;
            }

            .feature-list li {
                padding-top: 8px;
                padding-bottom: 8px;
            }

            .feature-list li .check {
                color: #167850; /* --color-success */
                font-weight: bold;
                margin-right: 8px;
            }

            .user-info {
                background-color: #fdf3e1; /* --color-warning-light */
                border-left: 3px solid #8e6014; /* --color-warning */
                border-radius: 8px; /* --radius-lg */
                color: #8e6014; /* --color-warning */
                padding: 12px;
                margin-top: 16px;
                margin-bottom: 16px;
                font-size: 14px;
            }

            a {
                color: #25293f; /* --color-primary */
                text-decoration: underline;
            }

            .footer {
                background-color: #eef0f4; /* --color-surface-hover */
                border-top: 1px solid #e9eaec; /* --color-border */
                padding: 24px 40px;
                text-align: center;
                color: #6e7180; /* --color-text-muted */
                font-size: 14px;
            }

            .footer p {
                color: #6e7180; /* --color-text-muted */
            }

            .footer a {
                color: #25293f; /* --color-primary */
            }

            .unsubscribe {
                margin-top: 16px;
                font-size: 12px;
                color: #6e7180; /* --color-text-muted */
            }

            /* Narrow-viewport (phone) tweaks. Padding for responsive
               elements is defined in the `<style>` block (not inline) so
               the media query overrides win on class-selector specificity
               alone, no `!important` needed. Clients that strip
               `<style>` will lose padding here, but those same clients
               don't process @media either, so the responsive layer is
               unaffected. */
            .email-wrapper-cell {
                padding: 20px;
            }

            @media only screen and (max-width: 620px) {
                .email-container {
                    width: 100%;
                    max-width: 100%;
                }

                .email-wrapper-cell {
                    padding: 12px;
                }

                .email-body {
                    padding: 24px;
                }

                .footer {
                    padding: 20px 24px;
                }
            }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" bgcolor="#eef0f4" class="email-wrapper">
<tr>
<td align="center" class="email-wrapper-cell">
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="600" bgcolor="#ffffff" class="email-container">
<tr>
<td align="center" bgcolor="#25293f" style="background-color: #25293f; padding: 24px; color: #ffffff" class="logo-cell">
{% comment %}
PNG, not the SVG this used to reference: Gmail, Outlook and Yahoo do not
render SVG in mail, so the mark was alt text for most recipients. The file
is rendered at 2x and flattened onto the same navy as this cell, since
alpha compositing is the other thing Outlook gets wrong.
{% endcomment %}
<img src="{{ base_url }}{% static 'img/sbomify-white-email.png' %}" alt="sbomify" height="40" width="214" border="0" style="color: #ffffff; font-weight: 600; font-size: 20px">
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="center" bgcolor="#25293f" style="background-color: #25293f; color: #d3d4d9; padding: 0 24px 20px 24px; font-size: 14px" class="tagline-cell">
The Security Artifact Hub
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="email-body">
{% block content %}{% endblock %}
{% block signoff %}
<p>
Cheers,
<br>
<strong>The sbomify Team</strong>
</p>
{% endblock %}
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td bgcolor="#eef0f4" align="center" style="background-color: #eef0f4; text-align: center; color: #6e7180; font-size: 14px" class="footer">
<p>
Questions? We're here to help. <a href="{{ base_url }}/support/contact/">Get in touch</a>
</p>
{% now "Y" as this_year %}
<p>© {{ current_year|default:this_year }} sbomify. All rights reserved.</p>
{% if unsubscribe_url %}
{% comment %}
    Only the onboarding sequence sets this. Account mail (billing, access
    decisions, token expiry) has nothing to opt out of, so it must not offer.
{% endcomment %}
<p class="unsubscribe">
Don't want setup tips? <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color: #6e7180">Unsubscribe</a>
</p>
{% endif %}
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
